                <pb facs="0566" n="556" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg556"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.3325/52: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-10-02T18:00:00-04:00">October 2, 1941—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>493. For the Under Secretary. Rossetti informed me this afternoon that our
                    request for permission for our war vessels to enter Chilean ports without
                    previous notice for refueling and supplies had been discussed with the heads of
                    the army and navy who are favorable but who ask that our tankers transfer fuel
                    to storage tanks in these ports and that our vessels refuel from them rather
                    than directly from our tankers. This to prevent possible attacks from political
                    opposition on charge ports being used as naval bases. It is asked too that the
                    agreement be made bilateral, not that any Chilean ships will avail themselves of
                    the privilege to be extended our vessels, but also to meet political criticism
                    in the event the agreement becomes public. He wants the agreement to be
                    confidential between the two Governments. He will ask the President for his
                    approval tonight.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
